          "number": 12,
          "letter": "L",
          "english": "It was only a year or so ago that Wardian realized that he had been a runner longer than a lacrosse player. It was not until he ran in the 2004 U.S. Olympic Marathon Trials-the first of three for Wardian-that he felt that he was a legitimate runner. Now more than 10 years and numerous ultra-marathon national titles and world records later, he embraces that identity. Wardian wants to see how far his legs can take him, one epic challenge at a time. \"I want to always keep doing things that are exciting, adventurous, different and most importantly, probably things I'm not the best at,\" Wardian said, \"because if you're not seeking things out that are challenging and difficult for you, then you're not growing … So I hope maybe people see what I do, and say, 'Okay, I want to do something different or try something new. … I'm going to do something that scares me.' That's what I'm hoping people will take from it.\"",
          "chinese": "大约直到一年前，沃迪安才意识到，自己从事跑步的时间已经超过了打长曲棍球的时间。直到参加2004年美国奥运会马拉松选拔赛——那是沃迪安参加的三次选拔赛中的第一次——他才觉得自己是一名真正的跑者。如今，十多年过去了，在赢得众多超马全国冠军并创造多项世界纪录之后，他已经接受了这一身份。沃迪安想知道自己的双腿究竟能带他走多远，一次完成一个史诗般的挑战。“我希望自己始终做一些令人兴奋、充满冒险、与众不同的事情，更重要的是，做一些我可能并不擅长的事情。”沃迪安说，“因为如果你不去寻找那些对自己来说具有挑战性和困难的事情，你就不会成长……所以我希望人们也许能看到我所做的事，然后说：‘好，我想做点不同的事情，或者尝试一些新东西……我要做一件让我害怕的事。’这就是我希望人们从中得到的启发。”",
